    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89-a1">

                <pb facs="0176" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg120"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Attachment]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the President</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-06">September 6, 1944</date>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d89-f1"
                        /></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the
                    President</hi></p>
                <p>As of possible assistance to you in your conversations with Mr. Churchill, I
                    attach memoranda concerning the following subjects:</p>
                <p>[Here follows a numbered list of the titles of ten Department of State briefing
                        papers.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d89-f2"/>]</p>
                <closer><signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ull</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d89-f1" n="1" xml:id="d89-f1-content">
                <p>The Department of State file copy of this memorandum bears the following
                    manuscript endorsement: “Sent to the White House 1:20 p.m. Sept. 8. J[<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">ames</hi>] E B[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >rown</hi>] <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jr</hi>.” (740.0011 E.W./9–644)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d89-f2" n="2" xml:id="d89-f2-content">
                <p>Annexes 4 and 5 to this memorandum are printed here. For annexes 1–3 and 6–10,
                    see <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg190">pp. 190</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg192">192</ref>, <ref target="#pg194">194</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg207">207</ref>, <ref target="#pg212">212</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg214">214</ref>, <ref target="#pg229">229</ref>, and <ref
                        target="#pg172">172</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
